      },
      "worked": "Replace $y\\mapsto \\frac{y}{3}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{y}{3}&=e^x\\\\y&=3e^x\\\\y&=e^{x+\\ln(3)}\\end{align*}$$\n\nReplacing $x$ by $x+\\ln(3)$ translates the graph left $\\ln(3)$ units.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
